# Launchpad Revived — working rules

## The spec is the source of truth

- `docs/spec/260730.01.md` defines every requirement. Read it before changing behavior.
- Deltas in `docs/spec/` with a later version number amend it and win where they conflict. The task prompt names which delta applies; read that delta in full before writing code.
- A delta's file-ownership section is binding. Files it marks out of scope belong to a separate work stream — do not edit them, and do not implement requirements outside the delta you were given, even if you can see them.
- Requirements have IDs (`WIN-03`, `DISC-07`, …) and status markers.
- **Implement `[D]` only.** Never implement anything marked `[O]` (open) or `[B]` (backlog), even if it seems obvious or trivially easy.
- Only work inside the currently active slice — see §12 of the spec.
- If a `[D]` requirement is ambiguous in a way that blocks you, **stop and say so.** Do not guess and do not pick a reasonable-seeming default.
- Never edit the spec file. Propose changes in your response instead.

## Build loop — build, do not launch

- **Agents build, they do not launch.**
- **`./run.sh --build` is the build command.** Run it after any code change.
- **Never run `./run.sh` without a flag, and never `open` the built app.** The app hides the menu bar and Dock system-wide (`WIN-03`), so launching it takes over the user's entire screen. Worse, an unrestored `presentationOptions` on a crash path leaves them with no menu bar and no Dock. Only the user launches this app, and only when present to watch it.
- If the build fails, read `.build/last-build.log`, fix the cause, and run again. Do not report completion on a failing build.
- Never invoke `xcodebuild` directly. Do not create additional build scripts — `run.sh` may be extended when explicitly asked, but it stays the only one.

## Non-negotiables

- Swift 6, strict concurrency. Deployment target macOS 26.0.
- Bundle identifier `lol.omg.rkm.LaunchpadRevived`.
- AppKit application shell (`NSApplicationDelegate` + custom `NSWindow`), SwiftUI content via `NSHostingView`. Do not restructure this.
- **No third-party dependencies.** System frameworks only. If you believe a package is needed, ask first.
- Liquid Glass via the system SwiftUI glass APIs. Never hand-roll a blur or vibrancy imitation.
- `os.Logger` for diagnostics, never `print()`. The sole exception is a diagnostic mode whose entire purpose is writing to stdout.
- One primary type per file, ≤ 300 lines. Split rather than append.
- Run `swift-format` before finishing.

## `presentationOptions` safety

`WIN-03` hides the menu bar and Dock. Every code path that can end a Launchpad session — dismissal, error, termination, crash handling — must restore the previous `presentationOptions`. Leaving a user with no menu bar and no Dock is the single worst failure this app can produce. Treat it accordingly.

## Commits

- One logical change per commit.
- Reference requirement IDs in the message. Example:

  ```
  Add app discovery scanner

  Implements DISC-01 through DISC-09. Uses .skipsPackageDescendants
  so embedded apps inside Xcode.app are not indexed (DISC-02).

  DISC-11 (Utilities seeding) not included — belongs with folders in Slice 3.
  ```

- When you finish a task, state which IDs you implemented and which you did not, and why.
